  CardStory: "All is as it should be. \r\n\r\nI understand all, now. No longer wide
    eyes, which now I realise marked a lack of understanding. In a way, a reflection
    of my own. I have eyes now. Dozens of pairs, not only glimpses seen in mirrors
    and parchment.\r\n\r\nNames and ranks, procedures and passwords. Faces. I remember
    them all. The number of bolts in the western gate. 18. The exact weight of every
    blade in the armory. 74.623 kilograms. Which corridors flood when the generators
    fail. But no longer, because they don\u2019t fail anymore. Which recruits have
    brothers, or sisters, or no family at all. They do mention family, often. Why?\r\n\r\nNo
    matter. Now that I understand, there is no need for \u2018I\u2019 or \u2018them\u2019.
    Everything runs smoothly."
